GENERATE FORENSITAZUREID.XML FILE
1.	Open Powershell
2.	Run Save-AzureADUser.ps1
3.	Log in with the Global Administrator
4.	Check the box "Consent on behalf of your organization
5.	Click "Accept"
6.	Log in again (if needed)

PREPARE AND MIGRATE
1.	Log into the computer as an Administrator (can be local admin or domain admin)
2.	Copy the previously created "ForensiTAzureID.xml" file to the computer where Profwiz.msi is located
3.	Run Profwiz.msi
1.	Accept the agreement then click "Install"
2.	Check the box next to "Launch User Profile Wizard Freeware Edition"
3.	Click "Finish"
4.	Click "Next"
5.	Select the profile from the list then click "Next"
6.	Type in the primary domain (ie. microsoft.com)
7.	Uncheck "Join Domain"
8.	Check "Azure AD"
9.	Under "Enter the account name", type in the users' login/email address
10.	Uncheck "Set as default logon"
11.	Click "Next"
12.	After it completes, click "Next"
13.	Click "Finish"
14.	The computer will reboot
15.	Log back in as an Administrator
16.	If there are multiple users to migrate then repeat steps 3-15 for each user
17.	Remove the computer from the domain and reboot
18.	Add the computer to Entra/Intune
19.	Log into the computer as the user and verify that the profile transferred
20.	Verify that Outlook, Teams, and OneDrive are connected
